# PLAN-5: Integrate centered + cosine/angular-margin prototype head into H-SFP (first accuracy fix)

## Current evidence (PLAN-3/4 diagnosis, cached round-1 baseline encoder, test-as-val)
- Root cause: encoder holds ~30% linear-probe signal but class MEANS are near-collinear (centroid
  cosine 0.985 at L1), so H-SFP's mean/Gaussian prototypes collapse (nearest-centroid 10.7%,
  mean/Gaussian ~6%). H-SFP baseline proxy val = 3.81% (stuck).
- Normalization factorial (normalize_results.json): centering collapses centroid cosine 0.985→~0.
  - centered + COSINE head: L1 21.41% (vs raw cosine 11.65%, vs mean-only 6.53%). L2 18.70%.
  - centered+whiten+L2 nearest-centroid: L1 25.58%, L2 26.56% (near the ~30% ceiling). Whitening
    adds ~4 pts but needs covariance/decorrelation (deferred).
  - centered+L2 ALONE does not lift nearest-centroid; the cosine head is what monetizes centering.
- Centering needs only a GLOBAL MEAN vector (= class-count-weighted average of transmitted prototype
  means) → ZERO extra transmission. Cosine head = cloud/edge-local change. Comms advantage preserved.
- full_e proxy was killed (hung ~80 min on epoch-1 client processing; number DNF — non-critical).

## Hypothesis (falsifiable)
Applying global-mean CENTERING to features/prototypes plus a COSINE/angular-margin classifier head
(L2-normalized features & class weights, learned scale) at the edge and cloud tiers — computing and
sampling prototypes in the centered space and applying the same centering+L2 to real features at
eval — will raise H-SFP proxy val top-1 from 3.81% to well into double digits (target ≥12%),
without any sample-level feature/gradient transfer and without extra per-round communication.

## Proposed isolated change
Add an ABLATION flag `prototype_space` ∈ {raw (default, = current H-SFP), centered_cosine}
(reserve `whitened_cosine` for a follow-up). `centered_cosine`:
1. Maintain a shared global feature mean μ per boundary, derived from the class-count-weighted mean
   of the aggregated prototype means (NO extra transmission). Subtract μ wherever prototypes are
   built/sampled and wherever real features are consumed (train + eval).
2. Replace the tier's linear classifier with a cosine/angular-margin head: logits = s·(ŵ·x̂) with
   L2-normalized x̂, ŵ and a learnable scale s (optional fixed margin m=0). Applies at cloud (and
   edge synthetic-supervised head if present).
3. Prototype summarization + diagonal-Gaussian/mean sampling happen in the centered space.

## Invariants
- `raw` default MUST reproduce the current H-SFP baseline exactly (preserve the original result for
  ablation). Guard with a config-hash/behavior check.
- No sample-level activation/gradient transfer. No extra per-round communication beyond μ derivable
  from existing prototype stats. Record any comms delta (expected ~0).
- Preserve uncommitted changes + all results; unique output dirs. Local only. Codex has no GPU →
  Codex implements + CPU unit-tests; Claude re-runs the proxy on host GPU.
- Do not modify baselines or default configs; add the flag, default off.

## Codex implementation tasks
1. Implement `prototype_space` flag in the H-SFP config + classification hierarchy; wire the global-
   mean μ estimation (class-count-weighted), centering at prototype-build/sample and at real-feature
   eval, and the cosine/angular-margin head with learnable scale. Keep memory/reliability/PRC/dropout
   compatible (they operate on the same centered prototypes).
2. Unit tests (CPU): (a) `raw` path is numerically unchanged vs current behavior (regression);
   (b) `centered_cosine` centers prototypes (post-center global mean ≈ 0) and the cosine head
   produces s·cosine logits; (c) train and eval apply the SAME centering (no space mismatch);
   (d) μ derives from aggregated prototype means with no new transmitted tensor.
3. Prepare a proxy config for `baseline_hsfp` + `prototype_space=centered_cosine` on the SAME
   partition/seed as PLAN-2 (reuse configs/proxy/plan2_cifar100_hsfp_baseline.yaml + --set), and emit
   the EXACT host-GPU launch commands for BOTH raw (control) and centered_cosine.
4. Note comms/VRAM deltas.

## Tests
1. CPU unit tests above pass; existing effect/regression suite still passes.
2. Both proxy configs resolve to distinct hashes; `raw` matches PLAN-2 baseline hash/behavior.

## Experiment matrix (Claude runs on host GPU)
CIFAR-100 proxy partition, seed 20260714, ~10 rounds; two runs: baseline_hsfp raw (control) vs
baseline_hsfp centered_cosine. Validation top-1 (test-as-val caveat noted). Sequential on host GPU.

## Promotion criterion (declared before running)
PROMOTE if centered_cosine proxy val top-1 ≥ 12% (>3× the 3.81% raw control) AND raw control
reproduces ~3.81%. On promotion: add whitening (whitened_cosine) as PLAN-6 for the extra ~4 pts,
then plan the held-out-val fix and a fuller comparison.

## Rejection/rollback criterion
If centered_cosine ≤ ~2× control (<8%), the pipeline integration loses the diagnostic gain —
investigate space-mismatch/eval-centering bugs (routine) before rejecting. If still no gain after a
verified-correct integration, reconsider: apply the cosine head at BOTH boundaries, or move to
whitening/encoder work (3A/3C). Keep `raw` intact regardless.

## Evidence Codex must return (compact)
- Filled EXECUTION REPORT; unit-test results incl. the raw-regression check; the two exact host-GPU
  launch commands; confirmed comms delta ~0; path to configs; unresolved risks.

